GooxGuuFDzjI_1oOrZuBAs=\",\"summary\":[]}"},{"type":"text","text":"[[reply_to_current]] **Current clinical picture**\nYou’re reporting **progressive exhaustion over the last few months**. From your stored record, I do see relevant background that could matter here: **hypertension**, **chronic kidney disease stage 2**, prior elevated blood pressure, and kidney markers that have worsened over time in the EHR context. Your DNA/genomic profile also suggests **higher predisposition to hypertension and CKD progression**, but genetics alone do **not** explain current fatigue without more symptom detail.\n\n**Preliminary interpretation**\nAt this stage, the more plausible explanations include **fatigue related to uncontrolled blood pressure or kidney disease burden**, **sleep disruption**, **medication-related tiredness**, or a more general issue such as **anemia, thyroid problems, low mood, infection/inflammation, or poor recovery**. I also do not want to miss higher-risk causes if the exhaustion is coming with **chest pain, shortness of breath, fainting, leg swelling, black stools, or rapid worsening**, because those would change the urgency immediately.\n\n**Recommended questions**\nAnswering a few targeted questions will help me narrow this down before giving you a fuller interpretation.\n**(1/4)** When did the exhaustion first start, and is it present all day or mainly at certain times (for example morning, afternoon, or after activity)?","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_0201feecf37c61400169d8d9c16f2881919270d95621f10afc\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":19094,"output":395,"cacheRead":1536,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":21025,"cost":{"input":0.04773500000000001,"output":0.005925000000000001,"cacheRead":0.000384,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.05404400000000001}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1775819196829}}
