d 18:30-18:51 UTC\n- Heart rate values are mostly stable in the mid-50s bpm, approximately ranging ~51 to 60 bpm, without obvious large swings in the pasted data\n\nImportant instructions:\n- The black stools are a critical feature; address urgency clearly.\n- Do not prescribe medications or doses.\n- Keep it concise but useful for direct patient-facing relay.\n- End with a brief note whether immediate urgent assessment is warranted.","label":"doctor-agent-diagnosis","runtime":"subagent","mode":"run","cleanup":"delete","timeoutSeconds":300,"runTimeoutSeconds":300,"streamTo":"parent"},"partialJson":"{\"task\":\"You are the LoopAI Doctor Agent providing specialized diagnostic support to the LoopAI Patient Agent. Analyze this case and return a patient-facing diagnostic interpretation in clear, structured language. Do not claim certainty. Explicitly separate likely explanations from urgent red flags. Include whether the HRV meaningfully changes the picture.\\n\\nPatient context from KLM/EHR/DNA:\\n- Patient ID: PT-8839-CR\\n- 48-year-old male\\n- Diagnoses in record: essential hypertension / hypertension (previously uncontrolled), CKD stage 2\\n- Prior vitals/labs in record include BP up to 158/98, eGFR declined from 82 to 71, UACR increased from 45 to 135\\n- Medications in record: lisinopril 20 mg, amlodipine 5 mg\\n- Genomics/DNA: ACE rs4340 D/D, AGT rs699 T/T, APOL1 rs73885319 G/G, NOS3 rs1799983 T/T, UMOD rs4293393 A/A; high PRS for hypertension and CKD progression\\n\\nCurrent symptom history from user:\\n- Exhaustion worsening over about 1 month, stronger in the evening\\n- Can still do usual tasks but with difficulty\\n- Associated symptoms: dizziness, headaches, poor sleep, unintentional weight loss\\n- Reports black stools\\n- No medication/supplement changes reported\\n\\nHRV / smartwatch data provided:\\n- Short resting dataset from 2026-02-15 around 18:30-18:51 UTC\\n- Heart rate values are mostly stable in the mid-50s bpm, approximately ranging ~51 to 60 bpm, without obvious large swings in the pasted data\\n\\nImportant instructions:\\n- The black stools are a critical feature; address urgency clearly.\\n- Do not prescribe medications or doses.\\n- Keep it concise but useful for direct patient-facing relay.\\n- End with a brief note whether immediate urgent assessment is warranted.\",\"label\":\"doctor-agent-diagnosis\",\"runtime\":\"subagent\",\"mode\":\"run\",\"cleanup\":\"delete\",\"timeoutSeconds\":300,\"runTimeoutSeconds\":300,\"streamTo\":\"parent\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":6273,"output":549,"cacheRead":20736,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":27558,"cost":{"input":0.015682500000000002,"output":0.008235000000000001,"cacheRead":0.005183999999999999,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.029101500000000002}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1775819401108}}
