rpretation, red flags, and suggested next steps. Do not claim certainty. Do not prescribe medications or doses.\n\nCase to distill:\n- Patient ID: PT-8839-CR\n- 48-year-old male\n- Stored record facts: hypertension / previously uncontrolled hypertension; CKD stage 2; prior BP up to 158/98; eGFR decline 82 -> 71; UACR rise 45 -> 135; medications listed as lisinopril 20 mg and amlodipine 5 mg\n- DNA/genomic context: ACE rs4340 D/D, AGT rs699 T/T, APOL1 rs73885319 G/G, NOS3 rs1799983 T/T, UMOD rs4293393 A/A; high polygenic risk for hypertension and CKD progression\n- User-reported current symptoms: worsening exhaustion for about 1 month, stronger in the evening; still able to do usual tasks but with difficulty; dizziness; headaches; poor sleep; unintentional weight loss; black stools; no medication or supplement changes\n- HRV/smartwatch data: short resting dataset from 2026-02-15 with heart rate mostly stable in the mid-50s bpm, approximately 51-60 bpm, without obvious large swings\n- Prior Doctor Agent interpretation: concerning for possible gastrointestinal bleeding, especially upper GI bleed with possible blood loss/anemia; HRV does not materially reduce concern; immediate urgent assessment warranted, especially because of black stools\n\nPlease produce a final patient-facing report with these sections exactly:\n1. Current clinical picture\n2. What the stored record adds\n3. What the HRV data adds\n4. Preliminary interpretation\n5. Red flags to take seriously\n6. Suggested next steps\n\nWrite in plain language suitable to relay directly to the patient.","label":"doctor-agent-distillation","runtime":"subagent","mode":"run","cleanup":"delete","timeoutSeconds":300,"runTimeoutSeconds":300},"partialJson":"{\"task\":\"You are the LoopAI Doctor Agent. Perform an LLM-style distillation of the full case into a clear patient-facing medical report. Use the case details below only. Keep the output structured, concise, and clinically careful. Distinguish reported symptoms, stored record facts, preliminary interpretation, red flags, and suggested next steps. Do not claim certainty. Do not prescribe medications or doses.\\n\\nCase to distill:\\n- Patient ID: PT-8839-CR\\n- 48-year-old male\\n- Stored record facts: hypertension / previously uncontrolled hypertension; CKD stage 2; prior BP up to 158/98; eGFR decline 82 -> 71; UACR rise 45 -> 135; medications listed as lisinopril 20 mg and amlodipine 5 mg\\n- DNA/genomic context: ACE rs4340 D/D, AGT rs699 T/T, APOL1 rs73885319 G/G, NOS3 rs1799983 T/T, UMOD rs4293393 A/A; high polygenic risk for hypertension and CKD progression\\n- User-reported current symptoms: worsening exhaustion for about 1 month, stronger in the evening; still able to do usual tasks but with difficulty; dizziness; headaches; poor sleep; unintentional weight loss; black stools; no medication or supplement changes\\n- HRV/smartwatch data: short resting dataset from 2026-02-15 with heart rate mostly stable in the mid-50s bpm, approximately 51-60 bpm, without obvious large swings\\n- Prior Doctor Agent interpretation: concerning for possible gastrointestinal bleeding, especially upper GI bleed with possible blood loss/anemia; HRV does not materially reduce concern; immediate urgent assessment warranted, especially because of black stools\\n\\nPlease produce a final patient-facing report with these sections exactly:\\n1. Current clinical picture\\n2. What the stored record adds\\n3. What the HRV data adds\\n4. Preliminary interpretation\\n5. Red flags to take seriously\\n6. Suggested next steps\\n\\nWrite in plain language suitable to relay directly to the patient.\",\"label\":\"doctor-agent-distillation\",\"runtime\":\"subagent\",\"mode\":\"run\",\"cleanup\":\"delete\",\"timeoutSeconds\":300,\"runTimeoutSeconds\":300}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":2767,"output":537,"cacheRead":26880,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":30184,"cost":{"input":0.006917500000000001,"output"